course: dictionary
lesson: 9499
title: Family words: stepbrother
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stepbrother is a boy or man who is the son of your stepmother or stepfather, but not the son of your own mother or father. Families come in many shapes, and many children grow up in a stepfamily. «Lucas, 9, moves in with Mum, his stepdad and stepbrother Jaylon, 11.» Jaylon is the son of Lucas's stepdad, not the son of Lucas's mum.
explain: Clues in a sentence help you work out who is who. «In Atlanta, Malachi's stepbrother Trey is the cool kid, and at school Trey ignores him.» Trey is Malachi's stepbrother, so Trey's parent has married or partnered with Malachi's parent, and the two boys do not share a parent.
explain: A stepsister is the girl version of a stepbrother. Being a stepbrother does not decide how someone behaves. «Mila's stepbrother teaches her to skateboard» shows that a stepbrother can be kind and helpful.
fact: A stepbrother is a boy or man who is the son of your stepmother or stepfather.
fact: You do not share a parent with your stepbrother, because he is not the son of your own mum or dad.
fact: A stepfamily forms when a parent marries or partners someone who already has a son.
fact: Stepfamilies are common, and families come in many shapes.
fact: «Older stepbrother» means a stepbrother who is older than you.
exercise: «In Atlanta, Malachi's stepbrother Trey is the cool kid.» Who is Trey to Malachi? | His brother from the same mum and dad | His best friend from school | His cousin | *His stepbrother, the son of Malachi's stepparent
exercise: «Mila's stepbrother teaches her to skateboard.» Which is true of a stepbrother? | He is always younger than you | He is always a baby | He has the same mum and dad as you | *He is the son of your stepmother or stepfather
exercise: Which word means the girl version of a stepbrother? | stepmother | cousin | *stepsister
test: «Lucas, 9, moves in with Mum, his stepdad and stepbrother Jaylon, 11.» Why is Jaylon Lucas's stepbrother? | Because Jaylon is older than everyone in the family | Because they have the same mum | *Because Jaylon is the son of Lucas's stepdad, not of Lucas's mum or dad | Because they go to the same school
test: In Wellington, «Mila's stepbrother teaches her to skateboard» and says «Sweet as, ya got it!» What does this show about him? | He is angry with her | *He is kind and helpful | He is a stranger she has never met | He is a teacher at her school
exam: In Dublin, «Amelia's stepbrother» says she is not his real sister, and it hurts. Why does this hurt her? | Because it is about the weather | Because it means she won a prize | Because it is a compliment | *Because it reminds her they do not share a parent, and she may feel left out
